      "rationale": "L6 explicitly names the junction as 'between D30 and T31'; Python verification confirms residue 30 = D and residue 31 = T in the canonical sequence. Both positions fall within the extracellular N-terminal span (1\u201338); the junction is 9 residues from the TM1 boundary (residue 39), well above the \u22653-residue minimum. No cysteines are present in the extracellular N-terminus (1\u201338), so no disulfide constraint is violated. The tolerated 8-aa HRV3C insertion demonstrates that this loop position accommodates a short peptide insert. Full-length V2R was engineered with a FLAG tag at the N-terminus and an HRV3C protease cleavage site (LEVLFQGP, ~8 aa) inserted between D30 and T31 of the extracellular N-terminal domain, along with a TEV site following the FLAG tag and a second HRV3C site at the C-terminus; the construct was expressed in insect cells and surface expression confirmed by anti-Flag M1 immunofluorescence (Alexa-488).",
      "residue_after": "T",
      "residue_before": "D",
      "residue_label": "D30",
