      "provenance": "literature_retrieved",
      "rationale": "AVPR2 has no signal peptide; residue 1 (M) is the first extracellular residue per the topology landmarks (1\u201338 extracellular). All N-terminal tag constructs in the ledger (L1\u2013L5, L8, L9, L13) use an exogenous signal sequence that is cleaved, leaving the tag immediately before V2R M1, making insert_after_residue=0 the only possible junction. L1/L2 provide the most explicit quantitative surface confirmation via the HiBiT cell-surface assay. The extracellular N-terminus is 38 residues long, providing ample space for a short tag. Full-length human V2R was N-terminally fused to an HA signal sequence followed by a FLAG-linker-HiBiT-linker cassette (MKTIIALSYIFCLVFADYKDDDDKGGSGGGGSGGSSSGGGVSGWRLFKKISGGSGGGGSG) in the pCAGGS vector; the HA signal is cleaved, leaving the HiBiT tag before V2R residue 1 on the extracellular face. AVPR2 has no endogenous signal peptide (topology residue 1 is directly extracellular), so the tag prepends before M1.",
